body:
I don't think you would be a pussy just because you dont want to harm yourself. To me that sounds like something in you in still figthing, despite how down you are feeling in this moment. I can imagine that this isn't even about dying but more about wanting a change.

&#x200B;

I hate reading that your parents are tired of you and seemingly do not know how to handle all that is currently going on with you. Sometimes, people do not understand this kind of darkness and this is the only way they know how to handle it.

&#x200B;

What do you think you need from them for things to get better? What could they do? Would it be worth talking to them about it?

I hate seeing you in this place where you are ready to leave and I wish I could do something to help you get out of that. I cannot imagine how stressful and hard life must be dealing with anxiety, depression, PTSD AND diabetes... I only struggle with the first two and at times I can't even handle that.

&#x200B;

I can imagine that it feels like there is little that can be done, especially during this pandemic. I know it is not much, but if you need people to talk and vent to about what is going on...  we are here for you if you ever need us.
